# Leading slashes matter here.
#
# These patterns are gitignore-shaped, so a bare `extension` matches a
# directory of that name at any depth — including `apps/web/src/app/extension`,
# the page that tells people how to install the recorder. It built fine and
# 404ed on the deployment, which is a difficult thing to explain from either
# end. Anchored to the repository root, every one of these means what it looks
# like it means.
#
# `apps/runner` is deliberately absent. It used to be here, on the grounds that
# a Playwright server cannot run on Vercel and including it only got it
# type-checked for nothing. That stopped being true when the site started
# running automations itself: the engine it runs is the runner's own, imported
# through `apps/runner/src/serverless.ts`.

/extension
/scripts
/suite-shots
/supabase
